<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seljuk Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Seljuks, Seljuk Turks, Great Seljuk Empire, Seljuk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Seljuk Empire, or Great Seljuk Empire, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Turkic state founded in the eleventh century by descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-warlord">Seljuk Beg</a>. It conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a> and defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manzikert">Manzikert</a> in 1071, opening <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> to Turkish settlement. It later fragmented into regional states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a>, and was a forerunner of the Khwarazmian and Ottoman empires.</p></div>
